# Live output of scripts/rederivation-sweep.sh while it is running.
#
# Ignored deliberately and only until the sweep finishes: committing a
# half-written arm would bank a truncated run as if it were data, and the
# dot-files below are the pristine copies of plant.rs / tree.ron that the
# script's EXIT trap restores from -- source backups have no business in
# git history.
#
# When PROGRESS reads SWEEP COMPLETE, `git add -f` the *_s*.log files and
# PROGRESS, and delete this file. The logs are the result and are meant to
# be committed; nothing else here is.
.plant.rs.orig
.tree.ron.orig
*.build
nohup.log
PROGRESS
*_s*.log
